# Z word on G5/G5.1 (BEZIER_Z_LINEAR) and exact G93 (BEZIER_EXACT_INVERSE_TIME).
# Numbers in [] are catalog IDs from ../../README.md. Every accepted curve is
# checked for a Z that never reverses and is linear in the length travelled
# (BEZIER_Z_LINEAR 2) or in the segment number (1), or off that line by no more
# than the firmware can tell from its estimates (3); zlen, zarc, zmm and zaim
# pin numbers.

# ---- end point and modes [50] ------------------------------------------------

= [50] Z word: G5 ends exactly at Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -11

= [50] Z word: G5.1 ends exactly at Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 Z2.5 I5 J5
pos -90 -100 -7.5

= [50] Z up and down along a chain, implicit I/J @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z3 I3 J3 P3 Q-3
G5 X20 Y0 Z-3 P3 Q3
G5 X30 Y0 P3 Q-3
pos -70 -100 -13

= [50] Z in G91 and inches @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G91 G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 P3 Q3
pos -80 -100 -12
G20 G5 X1 Y0 Z0.1 P0.1 Q0.1
pos -54.6 -100 -9.46

= [50] Z from a work offset far from the Z origin @z
G10 L2 P1 X0 Y0 Z-300
G0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z0.05 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos 10 0 -299.95

= [50] Z word outside the travel plane only with G17 @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G18 G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G19 G5.1 X10 Y0 Z-1 I5 J5 -> error
pos -100 -100 -10

# ---- Z against the path [51] --------------------------------------------------

# A straight line with both control points at its end: the parameter
# covers most of the length early, so Z by parameter runs far ahead.
= [51] handles 99:1 on a straight line, Z by length @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0
zlen 0 1e-5
zarc 0 1e-4

= [51] handles 99:1 on a straight line, Z by parameter is off by a third of the travel @zpar
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0
zarc 0.3 0.45

= [51] both handles at the start, quadratic with a far control point @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 Z-4 I40 J60
zlen 0 1e-5
zarc 0 2e-3
G5 X0 Y0 Z4 I0 J0 P30 Q30
zlen 0 1e-5
zarc 0 2e-3

= [51] loop and cusp: Z keeps climbing through the crossing @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z5 I20 J10 P10 Q10
zlen 0 1e-5
G5 X0 Y0 Z-5 I10 J10 P10 Q10
zlen 0 1e-5

= [51] symmetric arch: both variants within a tenth of the travel @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z1 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
zarc 0 0.1

# ---- float accumulation [52] --------------------------------------------------

# The length is summed in single precision over every segment, twice. At the
# cap that is 2000 additions of chords from 0.0002 mm to 30 mm.
= [52] 2000 segments: the running length stays on the line @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z50 I100000 J0 P1 Q50000
zlen 0 1e-5
G5 X0 Y0 Z-50 I0.01 J0 P100000 Q7
zlen 0 1e-5

= [52] 2000 segments far from the origin @zlen
G10 L2 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G0 X60000 Y-60000 Z-1000
F1000
G5 X60010 Y-60000 Z-1001 I30000 J0 P1 Q30000
zlen 0 2e-3

= [52] Z travel of one step on a long curve @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X300 Y0 Z0.004 I100 J100 P100 Q100

# Both control points on the end: the last chords are too short to count in a
# sum of 20 m, so the last points have the whole length behind them. The
# travel from Z-10 to Z0.3 has no exact float, and -10 plus it is past 0.3.
= [52] chords lost in the sum: Z waits at the target, never past it @zlen
F1000
G5 X20000 Y-100 Z0.3 I20100 J0 P0 Q0
G0 X-100 Y-100 Z-10
G5 X20000 Y-100 Z0.1 I20100 J0 P0 Q0
G0 X-100 Y-100 Z-10
G5 X20000 Y-100 Z7.77 I20100 J0 P0 Q0
G0 X-100 Y-100 Z-10
G5 X20000 Y-100 Z-0.7 I20100 J0 P0 Q0

# ---- degenerate curves [53] ---------------------------------------------------

= [53] all points coincide: a plain Z move, nothing divided by zero @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 Z-3 I0 J0 P0 Q0
pos -100 -100 -13

= [53] closed curve with Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 Z2 I10 J0 P0 Q10
pos -100 -100 -8

= [53] curve shorter than a step with a long Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0.001 Y0 Z8 I0.001 J0.001 P0.001 Q0.001
pos -99.999 -100 -2

# ---- Z by an estimate of the length ahead [57] [58] [59] ----------------------

# BEZIER_Z_LINEAR 3 makes one pass: every segment takes the share of the Z left
# that its chord is of an estimate of the length left. The estimate is halfway
# between the chords and the control polygons of some pieces of the curve, and
# the firmware vouches for BEZIER_SIGMA when that bracket is narrow enough.
# zaim pins the estimates made, those left too wide, and early ends of Z.

= [57] shallow Z: eight pieces are enough to vouch for 0.1 mm @zaim @!tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-0.5 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 1 0 0
zmm 0.002 0.0045
G5 X20 Y0 Z-3.5 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 1 0 0
zmm 0.012 0.027

= [57] shallow Z: sixteen to sixty-four pieces vouch for 0.002 mm @zaim @tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-0.5 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 3 0 0
zmm 0 0.0001
G5 X20 Y0 Z-3.5 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 4 0 0
zmm 0 0.0005

= [57] a handful of segments: the pieces are the segments, the length is exact @zaim
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X1 Y0 Z2 I0.3 J0.8 P0.3 Q-0.8
zlen 0 1e-4

= [57] handles 99:1 on a straight line: Z by estimate stays on the line @zaim
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0
zlen 0 1e-3

= [57] loop, cusp and a far control point @zaim
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z5 I20 J10 P10 Q10
zlen 0 5e-3
G5 X0 Y0 Z-5 I10 J10 P10 Q10
zlen 0 5e-3
G5.1 X10 Y0 Z-4 I40 J60
zlen 0 5e-3

# Steep Z: sixty-four pieces are still too wide, so the length is estimated again
# with half of the segments left, and again, until the pieces are the segments.
= [58] steep Z on a long curve: estimates left open, made again on the way @zaim @!tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X1000 Y0 Z-500 I300 J1200 P300 Q-1200
zaim 7 1 0
zmm 0.004 0.02

= [58] steep Z: estimates left open, made again on the way @zaim @tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-9 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 7 1 0
zmm 0.0001 0.0008
G5 X20 Y0 Z-39 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 8 1 0
zmm 0.0004 0.0025

= [58] steeper Z on few segments: the pieces double up to the segments @zaim @!tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-9 I3 J12 P3 Q-12
zaim 3 0 0
zlen 0 1e-5

= [58] the segment cap with Z @zaim
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z50 I100000 J0 P1 Q50000
zlen 0 1e-4
G5 X0 Y0 Z-50 I0.01 J0 P100000 Q7
zlen 0 1e-3

# Both control points on the end: the last chords are far shorter than what any
# estimate of 20 m is off by, so Z is at its target before the curve is.
= [59] chords shorter than the estimate is off: Z ends early, never past the target @zaim
F1000
G5 X20000 Y-100 Z0.3 I20100 J0 P0 Q0
zaim 1 0 1
G0 X-100 Y-100 Z-10
G5 X20000 Y-100 Z-0.7 I20100 J0 P0 Q0
zaim 1 0 1

# A handle straight out and back, with the turn inside one of the eight pieces:
# the estimate is short of the polyline, so the length runs out before the curve
# does. Z is then at its target; going on would take it past and back.
= [59] estimate short of the polyline: Z ends early, not past the target @zaim @!tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 Z-3 I0 J-131 P0 Q0
zaim 1 0 1
zmm 0.01 0.025

# Both control points on the start: the first chord is too short to take any of
# the Z left, and from Z0.3 to Z-10 the travel has no exact float. Without a hair
# less than all of it left, the first point would be above the start.
= [59] first chord too short to count: Z does not start backwards @zaim
G0 Z0.3
F1000
G5 X-20000 Y-100 Z-10 I0 J0 P19900 Q0
G0 X-100 Y-100 Z0.1
G5 X-20000 Y-100 Z-10 I0 J0 P19900 Q0
G0 X-100 Y-100 Z7.77
G5 X-20000 Y-100 Z-10 I0 J0 P19900 Q0

# 60 m out the float grid is 0.004 mm. The estimate runs between the same rounded
# points as the polyline, so the grid is in both and not between them.
= [59] far from the origin, on a coarse float grid @zaim
G10 L2 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G0 X60000 Y-60000 Z-1000
F1000
G5 X60010 Y-60000 Z-1001 I30000 J0 P1 Q30000
zlen 0 5e-4
G5 X60010.5 Y-60000 Z-1004 I0.3 J0.5 P0.2 Q0.5

# ---- the length estimated is the length travelled [61] -------------------------

# The last point of the polyline is the target, bit for bit. Horner's rule at
# t = 1 lands next to it on the float grid: -ffast-math regroups P3 - 3 P2 +
# 3 P1 - P0 into sums of four times the machine coordinate, whose grid is four
# times as coarse. An estimate that ended there was off by that step, and with
# L travelled and R estimated every Z is off by dz * x * (L - R) / (R * L).
# P0 = P1 = P2 at machine X-100 and P3 1025 float steps of 7.63e-6 mm further
# make two segments of 128 and 897 steps, and the estimate takes every point.
# Ending one step short, at 1024, put the middle at 128/1024 of 100 mm instead
# of 128/1025: 0.0122 mm off, six times $12. With the estimate ending at the
# target, the rounding of two sums is left.
= [61] the estimate ends at the target: no float step of XY in the length @zaim @tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-0.00782 Y0 Z100 I0 J0 P0.00782 Q0
zaim 1 0 0
zmm 0 0.0002

# The same curve where the grid is fine enough for Horner's rule to end on the
# target anyway.
= [61] the same curve at the machine origin @zaim @tol
G10 L2 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G0 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-0.00782 Y0 Z100 I0 J0 P0.00782 Q0
zaim 1 0 0
zmm 0 0.0002

# The first pass of BEZIER_Z_LINEAR 2 summed its last chord up to Horner's rule
# at t = 1 as well. On a curve 0.04 mm long at machine X-100 Y-100 a float step
# of 7.63e-6 mm is 2e-4 of the length, and so of the 60 mm of Z: 0.019 mm off
# measured, and 0.0097 mm on the quadratic, before that pass ended at the target.
= [61] two passes: the first ends at the target as well @zlen @tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-0.0313 Y0.0171 Z-60 I0.0111 J0.0237 P0.0071 Q-0.0133
zmm 0 0.0002
G0 X0 Y0 Z0
G5.1 X0.02 Y0.013 Z40 I0.017 J-0.006
zmm 0 0.0002

# B(t) = -10000 t^3 along X: the chords and the control polygons of eight pieces
# are the same 10 m, so the first estimate vouches for all of the segments, 2000
# of them with $12 at 0.002. Each takes its share of the length and of the Z
# left; their rounding is all there is, in 1 m of Z.
= [61] every segment updates the length and the Z left: rounding only @zaim
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10000 Y0 Z1000 I0 J0 P10000 Q0
zaim 1 0 0
zmm 0 0.002

# ---- exact G93 [39] [54] ------------------------------------------------------

= [39] G93 G5 takes 1/F minutes @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2

= [39] G93 G5.1 takes 1/F minutes @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 J5 F2

= [54] G93 with Z: the time covers the 3D length @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 Z-20 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2
G5.1 X20 Y0 Z0 I5 J5 F0.5

= [54] G93 with unequal segments and at the cap @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0 F4
G5 X110 Y0 Z50 I100000 J0 P1 Q50000 F0.01

= [54] G93 pure Z move through G5 @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X0 Y0 Z-3 I0 J0 P0 Q0 F2
pos -100 -100 -13

= [54] G93 does not leak: G94 after the curve, G1 in G93 @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2
G1 X20 F2
G94
F1000
G5 X30 Y0 Z1 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -70 -100 -9

# ---- G93 by estimate [60] ------------------------------------------------------

# With BEZIER_Z_LINEAR 3 the feed is taken from the first estimate of the length:
# the time is off 1/F by no more than its bracket, which every G93 curve is
# checked for. A curve of one segment keeps the inverse time of its only block.
= [60] G93 by estimate: one feed, time within the bracket @zaim @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J12 P3 Q-12 F2
G5 X20 Y0 Z-20 I3 J12 P3 Q-12 F2
G5 X20.001 Y0 Z-12 I0.001 J0.001 P0.001 Q0.001 F2
pos -79.999 -100 -22
